<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ordino</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ordino is one of the seven parishes of Andorra and the name of its main village, in the north of the principality on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valira">Valira</a> del Nord. Long a centre of iron working and of wealthy landowning families, it preserves the Casa d'Areny-Plandolit, home of the family of Guillem d'Areny-Plandolit, leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nova-reforma">Nova Reforma</a> of 1866, and includes the Sorteny valley nature park.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ordino.jpg" alt="Ordino" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Matthew Ross · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HPIM0307.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
